centralauth-login-error-locked:
{{Optional}}
Overrides CentralAuth's own message for a locked account, as a fallback. The usual route is this extension's pre-authentication provider, which runs before CentralAuth's primary provider and replaces the login error entirely.

An account can also be locked by a steward for reasons that have nothing to do with Trust & Safety, and CentralAuth's own message offers no route to anywhere at all. So this is hedged ("if Trust & Safety locked it") and points at Special:SafetyAppeal without asserting who locked the account or why.
